---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Corrections Policy | Aging at Home Lab" description="How Aging at Home Lab handles corrections, updates, outdated information, and safety-sensitive content changes.">
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Corrections Policy</p>
    <h1>How we handle updates and corrections.</h1>
    <p>Aging at Home Lab covers topics where clarity and caution matter. If a guide contains an error, outdated information, unsafe implication, unclear disclosure, or unsupported claim, it should be corrected.</p>

    <h2>What we correct</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Incorrect factual claims</li>
      <li>Outdated product, policy, or program information</li>
      <li>Unclear safety language</li>
      <li>Missing or weak source support</li>
      <li>Missing affiliate or sponsorship disclosure</li>
      <li>Guidance that could be misread as individualized professional advice</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Review dates</h2>
    <p>Guides should include review or update notes when relevant. Product-heavy, policy-heavy, and safety-sensitive pages should be reviewed more often than evergreen organization templates.</p>

    <h2>How updates should be handled</h2>
    <p>When a meaningful correction is made, the page should be updated with clearer language, stronger sourcing, or a new review date where appropriate. If a topic becomes too sensitive to cover safely without expert review, it should be held as draft or revised to focus on questions to ask qualified professionals.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
